window.SEARCH_INDEX = [{"title":"M-tel","url":"index.html","text":"Connecting Minds Around the World A Plan to Fit Your Needs M - Tel Networks (P) Ltd is a leading technology-driven Internet Service Provider (ISP) Request A Quote Check Availability Speed Test Uninterrupted internet Fibernet Broadband Leased Line Wireless Clients Our Plans Give You More Than Ever Request A Quote About Us M - Tel Networks (P) Ltd is a leading technology-driven Internet Service Provider (ISP), Established, in 2013, formed by a team of professionals to provide complete customer solutions. We provide uninterrupted and timely flow of information and our solutions facilitate decision making and sharpen your competitive edge by compressing time to market.. M - Tel Networks aims at offering high-quality Internet and Intranet on Wireless Technology. Internet, today is the basic need for communication, information, and education. It has wide acceptance in our society. The technology that we have implemented provides a high-speed and cost-effective internet connection to people. Read More.. What We Offer Services Fibernet View More... Broadband View More... Leased Line View More... Wireless View More... Intranet / VPN View More... Lan / Wan Networks View More... Real-Time Performance Connection Speed Test Benchmark your real-time latency, jitter, download, and upload speeds against M-Tel's low-latency optical gateway. Optimal Gateway: M-Tel Networks Core — Coimbatore (Tier-1 Peering) Network Status: Ready IDLE 0.0 Mbps Start Speed Test Ping / Latency -- ms Jitter: -- ms Download Speed -- Mbps Peak: -- Mbps Upload Speed -- Mbps Peak: -- Mbps Excellent Network Connection Your connection is suitable for 4K/8K Ultra HD streaming, low-ping esports, and multi-device cloud operations. Check M-Tel Fiber In Your Area Test Again Our Work Selected Work Dedicated circuit. Always active. Leased Line · LAN / WAN · Intranet / VPN Always-on connectivity for a multi-office team One dedicated circuit. Offices joined into one network. A monthly cost fixed at the start. The situation What we did What changed A normal dial-up connection is not always active. It shares the line, and the quality is hard to promise. When two offices need to work as one network, that uncertainty gets in the way. Specified the leased line between the endpoints. Set distance and speed; that fixed the monthly fee. Joined the offices with LAN / WAN and secured remote access with VPN. The connection stays active. It carries no other communications, so the carrier can assure the promised quality. Internal systems stay behind a firewall, and authorized users reach them through encryption. Distance and speed set the fee. Private network. Controlled access. Request A Quote Client Feedback What Clients Say “M-Tel’s dedicated fiber leased line gives our engineering campus continuous sub-2ms latency to cloud regions. The 99.9% uptime SLA has held solid without a glitch.” KS K. Senthilkumar Head of Infrastructure, IT Park, Saravanampatti Enterprise 1:1 Leased Line Subscriber “Switched from a legacy provider to M-Tel Fibernet. Our multi-branch retail network, VoIP, and billing systems now communicate over an encrypted private Intranet with zero packet drops.” RM R. Meenakshi Sundaram Operations Director, Retail & Logistics, RS Puram Multi-Office Intranet & Fibernet Subscriber “Providing high-speed Wi-Fi across our campus labs and administrative blocks was seamless. The site survey and fiber pull were completed on schedule without disrupting classes.” VA Dr. V. Anand Campus Administrator, Educational Institute, Peelamedu Campus High-Speed FTTH Subscriber NEW INTERNET PACKAGES ARE HERE! Subscription Plans High-speed optical fiber plans designed for uninterrupted home entertainment and mission-critical business connectivity. Home Fibernet Commercial &amp; Enterprise 100 Mbps STANDARD PLAN Cost-effective high-speed connection for streaming, browsing, and work-from-home. ₹ 699 / month Unlimited High-Speed Data Symmetrical Download / Upload Dual-Band Wi-Fi Router on 6mo+ 24/7 Dedicated Support Choose Standard Most Popular 250 Mbps SILVER PLAN Ultra-fast fiber designed for simultaneous 4K/8K streaming, smart homes &amp; gaming. ₹ 999 / month Unlimited High-Speed Data (No FUP) Gigabit Dual-Band Wi-Fi 6 Router Zero Installation Fee on 3mo+ Low Latency Gaming Routing Choose Silver 500 Mbps GOLD PLAN Pro-grade bandwidth for heavy home labs, creators, and executive offices. ₹ 1,499 / month True 500 Mbps Symmetric Optical Link Static IPv4 Address on Request Priority Enterprise Peering Routes 4-Hour Rapid Response SLA Choose Gold 1:1 CIR DEDICATED LEASED LINE 1:1 unshared committed information rate with strict latency SLAs for corporate offices. Custom SLA Guaranteed 99.95% Network Uptime Symmetrical CIR (10 Mbps to 1 Gbps) Static IP Subnet (/29 Allocated) 2-Hour Mean Time to Restore (MTTR) Request Leased Line Quote Corporate Ready MPLS / SD-WAN INTRANET &amp; MANAGED VPN Connect multi-location branches, warehouses &amp; retail hubs over an isolated private backbone. Enterprise Ring Zero Public Internet Exposure / Air-Gapped Hardware Firewall &amp; AES-256 Encryption Seamless LAN / WAN Interconnect Dedicated Account Executive &amp; Priority NOC Request VPN Architecture Fixed Wireless CAMPUS POINT-TO-POINT Long-range radio transceiver link for colleges, industrial estates, and remote facilities. Turnkey Setup No Physical Road Digging Required High-Throughput Microwave Transceiver Primary or Failover Redundant Link Free Site Survey by RF Engineers Schedule Site Survey Fiber & Leased Line Availability Coverage Area Checker Check instant optical fiber feasibility in your area across Coimbatore and Western Tamil Nadu. Search by PIN Code or Area Name: &times; Check Availability Popular Hubs: Saravanampatti (IT Park) RS Puram Gandhipuram Peelamedu Race Course Vadavalli Saibaba Colony Direct Fiber Active Ring: Alpha Core-1 Saravanampatti, Coimbatore — 641035 Ultra-fast FTTH Fiber Optic network and 1:1 dedicated enterprise leased lines are fully deployed and ready for immediate connection. Max Bandwidth Up to 1 Gbps Symmetric 1:1 Available Gateway Latency &lt; 2 ms Coimbatore Core Ring Service SLA 99.9% Uptime 24/7 Priority NOC Activation 24–48 Hours Quick Site Survey Available Technologies: FTTH Fiber Broadband Dedicated Leased Line (1:1 CIR) Managed Corporate VPN / Intranet High-Throughput Wireless Backup Request Connection in this Area Or Call Direct: +91 73737 10071 Coimbatore Metro Optical Ring Optical Nodes Active Gandhipuram (Core) Saravanampatti (IT) Peelamedu Singanallur Eachanari / SIDCO RS Puram Vadavalli Thudiyalur 100% Optic Fiber Ring &lt; 3ms Metro Latency 1 Gbps Gigabit Backbone Exclusive Benefits ULTRA FAST High-speed and cost-effective internet connection. Client satisfaction Satisfy our clients, not to convince them. Security Enough security for external and internal threats. 24X7 Services Uninterrupted and timely flow of information. Clients Don't Hesitate Any More Get In Touch With Us Request A Quote"},{"title":"About Us","url":"about-us.html","text":"Home / About Us About Us About Us M - Tel Networks (P) Ltd is a leading technology-driven Internet Service Provider (ISP), Established, in 2013, formed by a team of professionals to provide complete customer solutions. We provide uninterrupted and timely flow of information and our solutions facilitate decision making and sharpen your competitive edge by compressing time to market. M - Tel Networks aims at offering high-quality Internet and Intranet on Wireless Technology. Internet, today is the basic need for communication, information, and education. It has wide acceptance in our society. The technology that we have implemented provides a high-speed and cost-effective internet connection to people. M - Tel Networks is one of the best Internet Service Providers operating in this region and the client base that we have and their satisfaction level will declare for the best wireless technology that we provide at an affordable cost. We offer high-quality, high speed, low cost and easy to use Internet connection for home-based users, small entrepreneurs, corporate users, and educational institutions, granting clients to explore the true potential of the Internet. Our services are flexible and scalable to keep pace with increasing Internet needs. We provide WI-FI connections for all users as per their requirements without any compromise in quality. A site survey will be done by technical experts in the scheduled area where the connection is required and the work will be done without any delay and disturbance to the occupants. Once the connection is provided the subscriber will have access to the internet with excellent speed and will feel the latest internet technology with crystal clear clarity. By using the latest broadband technology called 'fixed wireless', the transceiver will be mounted on the roof of the client's building and the transceiver will be positioned to the closest Base Station which will send and receive signals. The signal received by the subscriber-unit is sent through a wired cable to the building to reach either the computer or the network-switch in the office or institution. Security is required to protect your systems, accounts and banking details, etc. M - Tel Networks provides a secured internet service to its users, which is perfectly maintained by professionals. M - Tel internet service has enough security for any external and internal threats. Our users need not worry while using bank details and accessing any confidential information over the web because of the strong security system provided to them. Why M - Tel Networks ? In M - Tel Networks we apply our expertise in making the latest Internet technologies to work effectively as per the client's needs. M - Tel Networks will support your organization by offering resourceful network, security and application services that will increase the usage and reduce the cost with the collective efficiencies. We use our expertise, mature processes and experience to set the standards to this organization in pursuit of our mission of ensuring customer satisfaction. Mission Our mission is to provide uninterrupted internet with low latency to all our clients as well as cost-effective and friendly customer service. We use only the finest quality products for our infrastructure as well as for installation and delivery. Vision Our vision is to \"satisfy our clients, not to convince them\". We believe that our next generation services will transform the way client's live, transact, and communicate. We trust that we can make a significant contribution towards a powerful Broadband all over our service area. Why we are here? M - Tel Networks always aims to deliver what we commit to our clients. We create an environment of endless learning and improving to improve the quality of work to give a better customer experience.A unique technology-driven Company focusing on Internet users with a vision to enrich the general public towards the i-world and offering affordable services. Why M - Tel Networks? Key Factors 01 Technology-driven We apply our expertise in making the latest Internet technologies to work effectively as per the client's needs. 02 Established in 2013 Formed by a team of professionals to provide complete customer solutions. 03 Uninterrupted, low latency We provide uninterrupted and timely flow of information, with low latency for all our clients. 04 Flexible and scalable Our services are flexible and scalable to keep pace with increasing Internet needs. 05 Site survey first A site survey will be done by technical experts in the scheduled area where the connection is required and the work will be done without any delay and disturbance to the occupants. 06 Security by design M - Tel internet service has enough security for any external and internal threats. A VPN secures the private network by using encryption."},{"title":"Services","url":"services.html","text":"Home / Services Services Services Fibernet Broadband Leased Line Wireless Intranet / VPN LAN / WAN Networks 01 / 06 Fibernet Fibernet is an Internet connection that transfers data fully or partially via fiber optic cables. Fiber refers to the thin glass wires inside the insulated cable. Optic refers to the way the type of data transferred (through light signals). It gives you virtually unlimited bandwidth capability, and it is the best technology on the market today. Fiber optic cables Light signals Virtually unlimited bandwidth 02 / 06 Broadband Broadband is used to describe a type of data transmission in which a single medium can carry several channels at once. Broadband is a radio term which means that multiple frequency carriers are used to carry one signal. It explains the way ADSL services work and so has become a term to describe a fast internet connection. Several channels at once Multiple frequency carriers Fast internet connection 03 / 06 Leased Line Leased lines are used by businesses to connect offices which are geographically distant. Dissimilar to normal dial-up connections, a leased line will always be active. The fee for this leased line connection will be fixed on monthly basis. Basic factors that affects the monthly fee are distance between the end points and the speed of the fixed circuit. This is because the connection doesn't carry any other communications and the carrier can assure the promised quality. Always active Fixed monthly fee Distance and speed set the fee 04 / 06 Wireless In networking terms, wireless is the word used to describe any computer network where there will be no physical wire connection between the sender and the receiver, but the network will be connected by the radio waves or microwaves to maintain communications. Wireless networking uses specific types of equipment, such as NICs, APs, and routers in the place of wires for connectivity. No physical wire Radio waves or microwaves NICs, APs and routers 05 / 06 Intranet / VPN The intranet is a private network that is based on TCP/IP protocols. The intranet is associated with an organization, usually a corporation, which is accessible only by the members of that particular organization, employees, or others with authorization. Intranet's websites and software applications look and act just like any others, but the firewall surrounding an intranet rejects unauthorized access. A virtual private network (VPN) is a network that is constructed using public wires which is usually the Internet to connect remote users or regional offices to a company's private, internal network. A VPN secures the private network by using encryption and other security systems to make sure that only the authorized users can access the network and no data can be intercepted. Private network Firewall Encryption 06 / 06 Lan / Wan Networks A local-area network (LAN) is a network that covers a small area. Mostly, a LAN is restricted to a single room or group of buildings, however, a LAN can be connected to other LANs over any distance through telephone lines and radio waves. A system of LANs connected together is called as a wide-area network (WAN). The difference between a LAN and WAN is that the wide-area network covers a relatively large geographical area. Typically, a WAN consists of two or more local-area networks (LANs) and are often connected through public networks. Small area LANs connected over distance Two or more LANs Questions Frequently Asked Questions What services does M-Tel offer? Fibernet, Broadband, Leased Line, Wireless, Intranet / VPN and LAN / WAN Networks. M - Tel Networks is a technology-driven Internet Service Provider offering high-quality Internet and Intranet on wireless technology. How is a fixed wireless connection installed? A site survey is done by technical experts in the scheduled area where the connection is required. The transceiver is mounted on the roof of the client's building and positioned to the closest Base Station, which sends and receives signals. The signal then travels by cable to the computer or network switch in the office or institution. How is a leased line different from a normal dial-up connection? A normal dial-up connection is not always active and shares the line. A leased line will always be active and does not carry other communications, so the carrier can assure the promised quality. The monthly fee is fixed by the distance between the endpoints and the speed of the circuit. Can M-Tel connect more than one office? Yes. Leased lines are used by businesses to connect offices which are geographically distant. LAN / WAN services join offices into one network, and VPN uses encryption so authorized users can reach the private internal network. Is the internet connection secure? M - Tel provides a secured internet service maintained by professionals, with enough security for external and internal threats. For private networks, a firewall rejects unauthorized access and VPN traffic is encrypted. Can the service grow as our needs change? Our services are flexible and scalable to keep pace with increasing Internet needs. Fibernet, for example, offers virtually unlimited bandwidth capability. How do I request a quote? Use the Contact Us form. Contact Us"},{"title":"Contact Us","url":"contact-us.html","text":"Home / Contact Us Contact Us Kindly Contact Us E-mail: md@mtelnetworks.com Phone: +91-73737 10071 / 72 Don't Hesitate Any More Get In Touch With Us Inquiry Details: Full Name * Email address * Phone No * Message Captcha Code send us"},{"title":"Clients","url":"clients-list.html","text":"Home / Clients Clients Enterprise & Institutional Trust Our Trusted Partners Over 10+ years providing robust fiber optic leased lines, intranet VPNs, and campus networks across Western Tamil Nadu. IT &amp; Software Parks 1:1 Symmetric Leased Line · 99.9% Uptime Healthcare &amp; Diagnostics Secure Medical Intranet &amp; Gigabit FTTH Manufacturing &amp; Textiles Multi-Site LAN/WAN &amp; Industrial Wi-Fi Colleges &amp; Universities High-Throughput Campus Microwave &amp; Fiber Logistics &amp; Retail Networks Point-to-Point VPN &amp; POS Telemetry Corporate Headquarters Dedicated CIR Circuits with 2h MTTR SLA Client satisfaction How Clients Benefit 01 ULTRA FAST High-speed and cost-effective internet connection. 02 Client satisfaction Satisfy our clients, not to convince them. 03 Security Enough security for external and internal threats. 04 24X7 Services Uninterrupted and timely flow of information. Our Work Case Study Dedicated circuit. Always active. Leased Line · LAN / WAN · Intranet / VPN Always-on connectivity for a multi-office team One dedicated circuit. Offices joined into one network. A monthly cost fixed at the start. The situation A normal dial-up connection is not always active. It shares the line, and the quality is hard to promise. When two offices need to work as one network, that uncertainty gets in the way. What we did Specified the leased line between the endpoints. Set distance and speed; that fixed the monthly fee. Joined the offices with LAN / WAN and secured remote access with VPN. What changed The connection stays active. It carries no other communications, so the carrier can assure the promised quality. Internal systems stay behind a firewall, and authorized users reach them through encryption. Distance and speed set the fee. Private network. Controlled access. Request A Quote Don't Hesitate Any More Get In Touch With Us Request A Quote"},{"title":"Privacy Policy","url":"privacy-policy.html","text":"Home / Privacy Policy Privacy Policy Policies Privacy Policy Cookies Policy Data Deletion Terms and Conditions Refund Policy Contact Us Draft — review before publishing. This page describes how this website works today and should be checked by M - Tel Networks before it goes live. Privacy Policy Information we collect When you use the contact form, we receive the name, email address, phone number and message you enter. The sign-in form collects the username and password you provide. The sign-up form collects your name, email address and password. A short-lived captcha cookie is set when the contact form is used, and embedded map content may set cookies through Google. How we use it Contact details are used to reply to your enquiry. Account details are used to sign you in or create your account. The captcha cookie helps confirm that a contact form submission came from a person. We use this information only for the purpose it was given for. Sharing We do not sell the details you submit. Embedded map content is served by Google, so that content is subject to Google's own policies. Our Cookies Policy explains the cookies involved. Your choices You can ask us to correct or remove the details you submitted. See our Data Deletion page for how to make that request. Contact Questions about this policy? Use the details below, or send us a message . E-mail: md@mtelnetworks.com Phone: +91-73737 10071 / 72"},{"title":"Cookies Policy","url":"cookies-policy.html","text":"Home / Cookies Policy Cookies Policy Policies Privacy Policy Cookies Policy Data Deletion Terms and Conditions Refund Policy Contact Us Draft — review before publishing. This page describes how this website works today and should be checked by M - Tel Networks before it goes live. Cookies Policy Cookies used on this site The contact form sets a captcha cookie named mtel_captcha . It holds the characters shown in the captcha image so that a submission can be checked. The cookie is set with HTTP-only and SameSite protection, and the captcha response is not stored for reuse. Embedded content Pages that show a Google Maps iframe load content from Google. That embedded content may set its own cookies, which are controlled by Google rather than by this website. Cookies we do not add This website does not add advertising or analytics cookies. Site search, navigation and page content run locally without tracking cookies. Managing cookies You can clear or block cookies in your browser settings. Blocking the captcha cookie may prevent the contact form from being submitted, in which case please use the phone or email details below. Contact Questions about cookies? Read the Privacy Policy , or use the details below to contact us . E-mail: md@mtelnetworks.com Phone: +91-73737 10071 / 72"},{"title":"Data Deletion","url":"data-deletion.html","text":"Home / Data Deletion Data Deletion Policies Privacy Policy Cookies Policy Data Deletion Terms and Conditions Refund Policy Contact Us Draft — review before publishing. This page describes how this website works today and should be checked by M - Tel Networks before it goes live. Data Deletion How to request deletion If you would like the details you submitted to be removed, contact us using the email address or phone number below, or use the contact form . Tell us which details you want removed and the email address or phone number you used, so we can find the right records. What happens next We remove the information from active enquiry records once it is no longer needed to respond to you or to provide and support a service. Some records may be retained where they are needed for billing, security or legal obligations. We will tell you if that applies to your request. Account details If you created an account through the sign-up form, include the email address used for that account in your request. This helps us identify the correct account details. Contact For deletion requests or questions, see the Privacy Policy or use the details below. E-mail: md@mtelnetworks.com Phone: +91-73737 10071 / 72"},{"title":"Terms and Conditions","url":"terms-conditions.html","text":"Home / Terms and Conditions Terms and Conditions Policies Privacy Policy Cookies Policy Data Deletion Terms and Conditions Refund Policy Contact Us Draft — review before publishing. This page describes how this website works today and should be checked by M - Tel Networks before it goes live. Terms and Conditions Using this website This website provides information about M - Tel Networks (P) Ltd and its services. You may browse it and use the contact, sign-in and sign-up forms for their intended purpose. Service enquiries Plan names and descriptions on this website are for information. Availability, pricing and the scope of a connection are confirmed directly with M - Tel Networks before a service begins. Submitting an enquiry does not create a service agreement. Accounts If you create an account, keep your sign-in details confidential and tell us if you believe they have been used without your permission. Information you provide through the forms is handled as described in the Privacy Policy . External content Map content on this website is provided by Google through an embedded frame. We do not control that content or its availability. Billing questions Questions about charges or adjustments are handled directly with M - Tel Networks. See the Refund Policy for how to raise them. Contact Use the details below or contact us with any question about these terms. E-mail: md@mtelnetworks.com Phone: +91-73737 10071 / 72"},{"title":"Refund Policy","url":"refund-policy.html","text":"Home / Refund Policy Refund Policy Policies Privacy Policy Cookies Policy Data Deletion Terms and Conditions Refund Policy Contact Us Draft — review before publishing. This page describes how this website works today and should be checked by M - Tel Networks before it goes live. Refund Policy Payments on this website This website does not take payment. Plan pages and enquiry forms collect enquiries only. Service agreements and billing are handled directly with M - Tel Networks. Raising a billing question If you believe you have been charged incorrectly for a service, contact us using the details below or send us a message . Include your account details and any payment reference so we can locate the correct record. How requests are handled Each request is reviewed against the agreed service terms and the records held for your connection. Any adjustment is discussed and agreed directly with you before it is applied. For the terms that apply to service enquiries, see Terms and Conditions . Contact For billing questions, use the details below. We also explain how submitted information is handled in the Privacy Policy . E-mail: md@mtelnetworks.com Phone: +91-73737 10071 / 72"}];
